{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef segment_tree_init(n):\n    size = 1\n    while size < n:\n        size *= 2\n    return [0] * (2 * size)\n\ndef seg_update(tree, idx, val):\n    i = idx + len(tree) // 2\n    tree[i] = val\n    i //= 2\n    while i:\n        tree[i] = tree[2 * i] + tree[2 * i + 1]\n        i //= 2\n\ndef seg_range(tree, l, r):\n    l += len(tree) // 2\n    r += len(tree) // 2\n    total = 0\n    while l <= r:\n        if l % 2 == 1:\n            total += tree[l]\n            l += 1\n        if r % 2 == 0:\n            total += tree[r]\n            r -= 1\n        l //= 2\n        r //= 2\n    return total\n\ndef prime_factors(n):\n    factors = []\n    i = 2\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            factors.append(i)\n            n //= i\n        i += 1\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n    return factors\n\ndef euler_phi(n):\n    factors = set(prime_factors(n))\n    res = n\n    for p in factors:\n        res = res // p * (p - 1)\n    return res\n\ndef mod_prod(a, b, m):\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(a + 1, b + 1):\n        res = (res * i) % m\n    return res\n\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\nphi_n = euler_phi(mod)\nlimit = n + 5\nfact_arr = [1] * (limit + 1)\nfor i in range(1, limit + 1):\n    fact_arr[i] = (i * fact_arr[i - 1]) % mod\n\nif n <= 3:\n    print(0)\nelse:\n    dp = [0] * 2000\n    dp[0], dp[1], dp[2], dp[3] = 1, 2, 2, 1\n    seg_tree = segment_tree_init(2005)\n    for i in range(4):\n        seg_update(seg_tree, i, dp[i])\n    current_max = 3\n    result = 0\n    for iter_num in range(n - 3):\n        prev_dp = dp[:]\n        accum = 0\n        for j in range(iter_num + 3):\n            for k in range(1, current_max + 2):\n                range_val = seg_range(seg_tree, j + k + 1, 2004)\n                accum = (accum + range_val * prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                seg_update(seg_tree, j + k, dp[j + k])\n        current_max += iter_num + 3\n        prod_val = mod_prod(iter_num + 3, n, mod)\n        result = (result + prod_val * accum) % mod\n    print(result)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static int[] segment_tree_init(int n) {\n        int size = 1;\n        while (size < n) {\n            size *= 2;\n        }\n        return new int[2 * size];\n    }\n\n    static void seg_update(int[] tree, int idx, int val) {\n        int i = idx + tree.length / 2;\n        tree[i] = val;\n        i /= 2;\n        while (i != 0) {\n            tree[i] = tree[2 * i] + tree[2 * i + 1];\n            i /= 2;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int seg_range(int[] tree, int l, int r) {\n        l += tree.length / 2;\n        r += tree.length / 2;\n        int total = 0;\n        while (l <= r) {\n            if (l % 2 == 1) {\n                total += tree[l];\n                l += 1;\n            }\n            if (r % 2 == 0) {\n                total += tree[r];\n                r -= 1;\n            }\n            l /= 2;\n            r /= 2;\n        }\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    static List<Integer> prime_factors(int n) {\n        List<Integer> factors = new ArrayList<>();\n        int i = 2;\n        while (i * i <= n) {\n            while (n % i == 0) {\n                factors.add(i);\n                n /= i;\n            }\n            i += 1;\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            factors.add(n);\n        }\n        return factors;\n    }\n\n    static int euler_phi(int n) {\n        Set<Integer> factors = new HashSet<>(prime_factors(n));\n        int res = n;\n        for (int p : factors) {\n            res = res / p * (p - 1);\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int mod_prod(int a, int b, int m) {\n        int res = 1;\n        for (int i = a + 1; i <= b + 1; i++) {\n            res = (int) ((long) res * i % m);\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] input = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(input[0]);\n        int mod = Integer.parseInt(input[1]);\n        int phi_n = euler_phi(mod);\n        int limit = n + 5;\n        long[] fact_arr = new long[limit + 1];\n        fact_arr[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= limit; i++) {\n            fact_arr[i] = (i * fact_arr[i - 1]) % mod;\n        }\n\n        if (n <= 3) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            int[] dp = new int[2000];\n            dp[0] = 1;\n            dp[1] = 2;\n            dp[2] = 2;\n            dp[3] = 1;\n            int[] seg_tree = segment_tree_init(2005);\n            for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n                seg_update(seg_tree, i, dp[i]);\n            }\n            int current_max = 3;\n            long result = 0;\n            for (int iter_num = 0; iter_num < n - 3; iter_num++) {\n                int[] prev_dp = dp.clone();\n                long accum = 0;\n                for (int j = 0; j < iter_num + 3; j++) {\n                    for (int k = 1; k <= current_max + 2; k++) {\n                        int range_val = seg_range(seg_tree, j + k + 1, 2004);\n                        accum = (accum + (long) range_val * prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                        dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                        seg_update(seg_tree, j + k, dp[j + k]);\n                    }\n                }\n                current_max += iter_num + 3;\n                int prod_val = mod_prod(iter_num + 3, n, mod);\n                result = (result + (long) prod_val * accum) % mod;\n            }\n            System.out.println(result);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.570780482841656e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00025722055579535663, -3.6238969187252223e-05, -0.5759835243225098, -0.4288792908191681, -0.00021598390594590455, -2.95634672511369e-05, -5.781483559985645e-05, -0.0003034608089365065, -3.933898824470816e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -4.362964682513848e-05, -0.061972882598638535, -0.0005547653418034315, -0.42014747858047485, -0.055707186460494995, -0.0025720868725329638, -0.456626832485199, -0.008660377003252506, -0.04886777326464653, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -0.0001662831346038729, -4.529942543740617e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.00014244495832826942, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.887569048150908e-06, -0.06994212418794632, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.5748875486897305e-05, -5.960446742392378e-06, -0.001503052655607462, -2.